### E.3 Community & Discussion Platforms

**Ziggit**
[ziggit.dev](https://ziggit.dev/)
The official forum for the Zig community. It is where language design discussions, release announcements, and deep technical questions live. The “Show and Tell” and “Zig in Production” categories are excellent for seeing what others are building and how they solved problems.

**Zig Discord**
[discord.gg/zig](https://discord.gg/zig)
Real‑time chat with active core team members and library authors. The `#zig-help` channel is surprisingly high‑signal for a Discord server — but as with any chat, do your homework first.

**r/Zig**
[reddit.com/r/Zig/](https://www.reddit.com/r/Zig/)
Subreddit for news, articles, and project showcases. Useful for discovering libraries that don’t yet appear on Awesome‑Zig.

**Awesome Zig**
[github.com/nrdmn/awesome-zig](https://github.com/nrdmn/awesome-zig)
Curated list of libraries, bindings, and tools. When you need a JSON parser, an HTTP library, or a cross‑platform GUI binding, start here before reinventing the wheel.

**Zig Showtime**
[YouTube playlist](https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLTcc2G-vUyKdQ4QLfRx8S0U_K7hn2Mk0j) (by Loris Cro)
Long‑form videos that walk through the compiler internals, building a Zig compiler from scratch, and deep dives into `build.zig`. They are unpolished but extraordinarily insightful for anyone who wants to understand the toolchain.

