### E.7 Further Reading & Keeping Current

- **Zig Language Blog**
  [ziglang.org/news/](https://ziglang.org/news/) — Release notes, status updates, and community highlights. Subscribe to the RSS feed.

- **“What’s Zig Got That C, Rust, and Go Don’t Have?”**
  Various community blog posts and conference talks that contrast the languages. Search for recent comparisons that include Zig 0.13+ features; older articles may reference the removed async/await model.

- **The Zig Embedded Group**
  [github.com/ZigEmbeddedGroup](https://github.com/ZigEmbeddedGroup) — Resources, linker scripts, and bare‑metal HAL libraries for microcontrollers. If you target Cortex‑M or RISC‑V MCUs, start with `microzig`.

- **Zig Monthly**
  A community newsletter (search for it on Ziggit) that rounds up new library releases, notable PRs in the compiler, and upcoming events. It is the most efficient way to stay informed without monitoring every repository.

---

The Zig landscape evolves quickly. The resources above are stable anchors, but always cross‑reference with the official documentation and the latest release notes. When you discover a new library or a groundbreaking talk, apply the same critical lens you use for your own code: does it respect **no hidden control flow**, is it **explicit over implicit**, and does it leverage **comptime** to push work to the compiler? If the answer is yes, that resource belongs on your shelf.
